# Frontend Standards

## Framework & Setup
- **Framework:** React 18+ with Vite.
- **Components:** Functional components with Arrow Functions only.
- **Styling:** Use Tailwind CSS utility classes.

## Styling Strategy - Keep JSX Clean

### Core Rule: Use `@apply` in `index.css` for Repeated Patterns

**When to use `@apply`:**
- Tailwind class strings longer than 3-4 utilities
- Patterns used in 2+ components
- Complex combinations (e.g., `p-4 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg border border-slate-800`)

**Naming Convention:**
- Use kebab-case for custom classes (e.g., `.card-container`, `.btn-primary`)
- Prefix with component name if component-specific (e.g., `.chat-input`, `.layout-sidebar`)

**File Location:**
- All `@apply` patterns go in `client/src/index.css`
- Keep JSX clean with semantic class names.

## Component Structure
- **Exports:** Use named exports: `export function ComponentName() {}`
- **Props:** Define TypeScript interfaces for all props.
- **File Organization:** One component per file, co-locate related files.

## Examples

### ✅ Good: Clean JSX with `@apply`

```css
/* client/src/index.css */
.card-container {
  @apply p-4 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg border border-slate-800;
}

.chat-input {
  @apply flex-1 resize-none bg-transparent text-sm text-slate-100 placeholder:text-slate-600;
}
```

```tsx
// client/src/components/UserProfile.tsx
import type { UserProps } from './types';

export const UserProfile = ({ name }: UserProps) => {
  return <div className="card-container">{name}</div>;
};
```

### ❌ Bad: Long Tailwind strings in JSX

```tsx
<div className="p-4 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-800 transition-colors">
  {name}
</div>
```

### ❌ Bad: Inline styles or function keyword

```tsx
<div style={{ padding: '1rem', backgroundColor: '#0f172a' }}>{name}</div>

function UserProfile(props) {
  return <div>{props.name}</div>;
}
```
